//? Title: Q-learning: actual behavior draws, targets and finite policy evaluation
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
An actual environment transition supplies the reward and next state; the native
update bootstraps from the greedy next Q value even when behavior explores. The
producer now records its real RNG branch, callback transition and scalar
before/target/after values. The original 4x4 grid,500 episodes, seed 42 and
20-episode return smoothing remain. A deterministic corridor first exposes the
mechanism; the grid then shows a finite training trajectory and a separate
actual greedy-policy rollout.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

$$ Q(s,a)\gets Q(s,a)+\alpha\{r+\gamma\max_b Q(s\prime,b)-Q(s,a)\};\qquad\text{terminal bootstrap}=0. $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/q_learning_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    a::RLParameters params;
    params.learning_rate = .5;
    params.discount = .9;
    params.epsilon = 0;
    params.episodes = 2;
    params.max_steps = 4;
    auto t = a::q_learning_trace(a::tabular_corridor(2), params);
    std::print("\n| actual episode | step | state | action | reward | terminal | Q before | actual target | " "Q after |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &s : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
                   s.episode, s.step, s.state, s.action, s.reward, s.terminal,
                   s.before, s.target, s.after);
    const auto &first = t.steps[0];

    g::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual selected Q before\n{}", first.before));
    d.node("n1", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual callback / TD target\nr={}, target={}",
                       first.reward, first.target));
    d.node("n2", {20, 0},
           std::format("Actual additive update\nQ after={}", first.after));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/q_learning_tiny.svg");
}
```
