> Actual selected work and sensitivity

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/q_learning_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("\n| explicit epsilon | actual transitions | exploratory selections | greedy selections | " "greedy rollout steps (cap100) | terminal rollout |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | " "--- |\n");
    for (double epsilon : {0., .1, .5, 1.}) {
        a::RLParameters p;
        p.learning_rate = .5;
        p.discount = .95;
        p.epsilon = epsilon;
        p.episodes = 500;
        p.seed = 42;
        auto env = a::tabular_grid(4);
        auto r = a::q_learning_run(env, p);
        auto rollout =
            a::tabular_policy_rollout(env, r.result.greedy_policy, 100);
        x.push_back(epsilon);
        y.push_back(r.transitions);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", epsilon, r.transitions,
                   r.exploratory_actions, r.greedy_actions,
                   rollout.actions.size(), rollout.terminal);
    }
    auto p = g::RPlot::create();
    p.lines(x, y, "actual transitions during 500 training episodes",
            {16, 122, 87}).points(x, y, {16, 122, 87}, 5).title(
        "Fixed native grid/seed: exploration changes actual collected training work").x_label("behavior exploration probability").y_label("actual environment transitions");
    p.save_svg("build/q_learning_work.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| explicit epsilon | actual transitions | exploratory selections | greedy selections | greedy rollout steps (cap100) | terminal rollout |
| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
| 0 | 3328 | 0 | 3328 | 6 | true |
| 0.1 | 3623 | 338 | 3285 | 6 | true |
| 0.5 | 5889 | 2908 | 2981 | 6 | true |
| 1 | 29493 | 29493 | 0 | 6 | true |
\image(figures/q_learning_work.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual selected event counts or represented numerical outcomes; raw values are retained in the computed table.)
\alttext(Actual selected event counts or represented numerical outcomes; raw values are retained in the computed table.)

> API and interpretation

A constant step size, constant exploration and a finite seed/run do not
establish the asymptotic Q-learning convergence assumptions. Training returns
belong to the exploring behavior policy; the separate fixed greedy rollout is
labelled as evaluation. The-6 line is an undiscounted shortest-path reference
for this deterministic grid, while Q values use discount. Smoothing is
descriptive and supplies no uncertainty interval. Callback side effects cannot
be rolled back; geometry, parameters and actual callback states/rewards are
checked before their respective uses. Zero-step episodes reset and are truncated
rather than falsely reported terminal.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Q-learning, Watkins and Dayan|https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00992698]

